FlashTerm: FLASHTERM_TTS_RENDER is not set to a runnable command.

It names the synthesiser, with {out} for the file to write and the text arriving
on standard input. For example:

  FLASHTERM_TTS_RENDER="piper -m fr_FR-siwis-medium -f {out}"
  FLASHTERM_TTS_RENDER="espeak-ng -v fr --stdin -w {out}"

There is no default because a voice implies a language, and guessing it would
render a French deck in English.
